The `-response` counterparts of these files (`level-1-response.json`, `level-2-response.json`, the level-3 batch variants and their `-response` files) are **not** vendored: this pack grades the API-call sequence only, and every scenario it evaluates is derived from the three files above. `scripts/generate-dataset.mjs` re-checks each file's SHA-256 before building anything, and the vendored SHA-256 values are recorded in the generated header of `lib/generated/scenarios.ts`.

The pack applies one deterministic transform at build time — API-definition extraction, per-step dialogue re-ordering and de-duplication, and Mock-result harvesting — which never mutates the vendored files. See [METHODOLOGY.md](METHODOLOGY.md).

